CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ member moved: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ move is non-throwing: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The implicit move constructor was declared only when a subobject was
move-only (declare_implicit_move in cpp_typecheck_compound_type.cpp), so
Holder(std::move(a)) called the implicit copy constructor, which copied
the member, and the noexcept operator read the copy constructor's
specification.  It is now declared, under the conditions of
[class.copy.ctor]/8, when a base or member has a move constructor; for
the other classes the memberwise move is the memberwise copy.
